{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.RibbonDH","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.RibbonDH","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.Twist","lean:module:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.Linear","lean:module:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.Duals","lean:module:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.BraidingVV","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RibbonHeckeDimension","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.qDim_V_eq_qint_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.qDim_V_eq_qint_two","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L241-L262","doc":"**S6: `dim_q V = [2]_q` in `D_ℏ`.** For `ℏ` transcendental and any associator `Ψ`, the ribbon\nquantum dimension of `V = ℂ²` in the Drinfeld category is `q + q⁻¹` with `q = e^{iπℏ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.id_V_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.id_V_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L235-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.end_unit_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.end_unit_eq","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L223-L232","doc":"`End(𝟙) = ℂ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.twist_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.twist_V","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L219-L221","doc":"**The twist of `V`** is the scalar `e^{3iπℏ/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.hecke_DH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.hecke_DH","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L212-L217","doc":"**The Hecke skein relation in `D_ℏ`**: `s·β_{V,V} − s⁻¹·β_{V,V}⁻¹ = (q − q⁻¹)·𝟙`,\n`s = e^{iπℏ/2}`, `q = e^{iπℏ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.Vd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.Vd","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L207-L208","doc":"`V` as an object of `D_ℏ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.aV_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.aV_eq","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L204-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.θmat_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.θmat_V","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L201-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.aV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.aV","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L198-L199","doc":"`e^{3iπℏ/2}`, the twist of `V` (`θ_V = q^{C_V}` with `C_V = 3/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.casimir_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.casimir_V","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L187-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.ribbon_hecke_dimension_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.ribbon_hecke_dimension_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L161-L176","doc":"**Scaled Hecke relation ⟹ dimension.** If `s·β − s⁻¹·β⁻¹ = (q − q⁻¹)·𝟙` on `V ⊗ V`,\n`θ_V = a·𝟙` and `dim_q V = d·𝟙`, then `((q − q⁻¹)·d)·𝟙_V = (s·a − s⁻¹·a⁻¹)·𝟙_V`. With `s = 1` this\nis `ribbon_hecke_dimension`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.ribbon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.ribbon","kind":"instance","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L139-L146","doc":"**`D_ℏ` is ribbon** (`ℏ` transcendental, any associator `Ψ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.twist_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.twist_val","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.balanced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.balanced","kind":"instance","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L118-L129","doc":"**`D_ℏ` is balanced**: `θ_X = exp(iπℏ Ω_X)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.θmat_mul_θinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.θmat_mul_θinv","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.θinv_mul_θmat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.θinv_mul_θmat","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L114-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eps_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eps_twist","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L100-L105","doc":"**The twist passes through an invariant pairing**: `ε ∘ (θ_Y ⊗ 1) = ε ∘ (1 ⊗ θ_X)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eps_casimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eps_casimir","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L89-L96","doc":"An invariant pairing `Y ⊗ X → 𝟙` sees the Casimir of `Y` as the Casimir of `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eps_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eps_pair","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L82-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.kron_one_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.kron_one_comm","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L77-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eps_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eps_flip","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L71-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eq_of_whiskerRight_comp_evaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.eq_of_whiskerRight_comp_evaluation","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/RibbonDH.lean#L46-L61","doc":"Precomposing the evaluation `ε : Y ⊗ X ⟶ 𝟙` with `g ▷ X` is injective in `g`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}